{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-isotope-knot-equivalence","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:isotope-knot-equivalence","kind":"proposition","title":"A reflexive, symmetric, transitive isotope relation is an equivalence","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-isotope-knot"],"tags":["equivalence-relation","isotope","atom-knot"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.IsotopeKnot.equivalence","text":"isotope-knot-equivalence.md","leanSource":"isotope-knot-equivalence.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:isotope-knot-equivalence\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sim</code> be a relation on atom-knots with fixed <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Z</code>, and assume that <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sim</code> is reflexive, symmetric and transitive. Then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sim</code> is an equivalence relation.</em></p>\n<p><em>Whether the isotope relation of <a href=\"#def:isotope-knot\" data-at=\"knots-particles-confinement/atom-isotope-knots\">9.10.5</a> satisfies these three properties is not part of this statement; they are hypotheses.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/isotope-knot-equivalence.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"9.10.7","page":"b/prop-isotope-knot-equivalence","qa":{"counts":{"pass":90,"fail":1,"warn":1,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":78},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsotopeKnot.equivalence","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/isotope-knot-equivalence.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
